  "why": "N18 (SSPN-74): the same library case as `package_join`, but `billing` imports from the package (`from shared import Money, to_cents`) and `shared/__init__.py` re-exports them from `shared.money`. Inside one repository a re-export resolves to the defining symbol; across a declared package join it used to resolve to the provider's *package* (`shared@shared`), so the two imports collapsed into one edge to a module and both calls landed on it: the same code gave two answers. The provider's re-export tables now travel with the join, so the imports and calls land on `shared.money.to_cents`, `shared.money.Money` and the classmethod `Money.of`. `json` is the control: genuinely third-party, it stays a placeholder.",
